   "subject": "geom_vline() not inheriting data within mean() function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m back with another NOOB question.</div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to get<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div>to use the data available in <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div>?</div><div><br></div><div>e.g.,</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> women</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mapping </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weight</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xintercept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><br>won&#39;t work but:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> women</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mapping </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weight</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xintercept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">women$height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div></div><div>will.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Timothy</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "qWQETrFbCwAJ",
   "from": "Timothy Lau",
   "author": "f3f87164b9c7de94",
   "date": "2017-08-15T20:23:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: geom_vline() not inheriting data within mean() function",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This is the same if you use dplyr:<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">women </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mapping </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weight</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xintercept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> summarize</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span></div></code></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><br>On Tuesday, August 15, 2017 at 2:16:59 PM UTC-6, Timothy Lau wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;m back with another NOOB question.</div><div><br></div><div>Is there a way to get<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div>to use the data available in <div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span></div></code></div>?</div><div><br></div><div>e.g.,</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> women</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mapping </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weight</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xintercept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><br>won&#39;t work but:</div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">ggplot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> women</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mapping </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> y </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> weight</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_point</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_vline</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">xintercept </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> mean</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">women$height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div></div><div>will.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Timothy</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
